<%# Questions about the document, laid out as a conversation: the reader's own
    words on the right, the answer on the left (D4). No avatars and no
    timestamps — a time would have to be rendered in the server's zone, which is
    the very thing the retention countdown exists to avoid (D4, R2.7).

    Attribution is text, not colour or position, so it survives a screen reader
    and a monochrome display alike (R2.6). The list stays an <ol> for the same
    reason: the order of an exchange is meaning, not decoration.

    Answers carry where they came from, so a reader can check rather than take
    them on trust. %>
<section aria-labelledby="ask-heading" class="mb-10">
  <h2 id="ask-heading" class="text-lead font-bold mb-5">Ask about this document</h2>

  <% if document.messages.any? %>
    <ol class="mb-8 space-y-4 list-none">
      <% document.messages.ordered.each do |message| %>
        <%# The id is what MessagesController redirects to, so asking a question
            lands the reader on the answer rather than the top of the page (R2.3). %>
        <li id="<%= dom_id(message) %>" class="flex <%= message.asked? ? "justify-end" : "justify-start" %>">
          <div class="max-w-[85%] sm:max-w-[75%]">
            <p class="text-body text-ink-muted mb-1 <%= "text-right" if message.asked? %>">
              <%= message.asked? ? "User" : "AI" %>
            </p>

            <%# Both colour pairs are already asserted for contrast in
                PaletteTest; break-words keeps a long unbroken string from
                widening the page, which the no-sideways-scroll test guards. %>
            <div class="rounded-2xl p-5 text-lead break-words <%=
                  message.asked? ? "bg-notice-bg text-notice-ink rounded-br-sm" : "border-2 border-rule rounded-bl-sm" %>">
              <%= message.content %>
            </div>

            <% if message.answered? && message.citations.any? %>
              <p class="text-body text-ink-muted mt-2">
                From <%= message.citations.to_sentence %> of your document.
              </p>
            <% end %>
          </div>
        </li>
      <% end %>
    </ol>
  <% else %>
    <p class="text-body text-ink-muted mb-8">
      No questions yet. Ask anything about what this document says.
    </p>
  <% end %>

  <%= form_with url: document_messages_path(document), method: :post do |form| %>
    <%= form.label :question, "Type your question", class: "block text-body mb-2" %>
    <%= form.text_field :question, required: true, autocomplete: "off",
          class: "block w-full text-lead border-2 border-rule rounded-lg p-4 mb-4" %>
    <%= form.submit "Ask",
          class: "w-full sm:w-auto rounded-lg bg-accent text-accent-ink px-8 py-4 text-lead font-bold cursor-pointer" %>
  <% end %>
</section>
